.TH QID 1 "2026-09-07" "qid 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qid \- look up a Qualys QID and optionally create a confirmed ignore
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qid
.RI [ QID ]
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
.B qid ?
.PP
.B qid \-\-man
.PP
.B qid
.I QID
.RB \-\-ignore
.RB [ \-\-ips IP_FILTER | \-\-asset-ids ASSET_IDS | \-\-dns-hostnames HOSTNAMES ]
.RB \-\-comment COMMENT
.RB [ \-\-reopen-after-days DAYS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queries Qualys host detections for one QID. If QID is omitted, an explicit
selector is required and all QIDs returned for that device are displayed.
With a QID and no selector, all assets returned by Qualys are queried; a
selector limits the lookup to a chosen scope.
Lookups and ignored-state verification are read-only. Creating an exception
requires \fB\-\-ignore\fR, an audit comment, and the exact confirmation
requested by the command.
.PP
An unscoped lookup may be a large and slower request. The \fB\-\-ignore\fR
workflow always requires an explicit selector.
.PP
Asset and hostname selectors are resolved through Qualys Host List data. The
tool then queries only exact IP addresses returned for matching assets; it does
not perform local DNS resolution.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI QID
Optional positive Qualys QID to query. Omit it to list all QIDs for an
explicit IP, Asset ID, or DNS/hostname selector.
.TP
.BI \-\-ips\ IP_FILTER
Comma-separated IPv4 addresses and/or ranges, for example
.IR 192.0.2.10-192.0.2.20 .
The alias is \fB\-\-ip\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-asset-ids\ ASSET_IDS
Comma-separated exact Qualys Asset IDs.
The alias is \fB\-\-asset-id\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-dns-hostnames\ HOSTNAMES
Comma-separated exact DNS names or hostnames. Matching is case-insensitive and
ignores a trailing dot.
The aliases are \fB\-\-dns-hostname\fR and \fB\-\-hostname\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-verify-ignored
Include detection-level ignored-state evidence in a read-only result. Cannot
be combined with \fB\-\-ignore\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-ignored-only
With \fB\-\-verify-ignored\fR, show only detections that Qualys reports as
currently ignored. This is read-only.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore
Submit an ignore request after preflight lookup and exact interactive
confirmation. This changes Qualys state.
.TP
.BI \-\-comment\ COMMENT
Required audit comment for \fB\-\-ignore\fR; maximum 255 characters.
.TP
.BI \-\-reopen-after-days\ DAYS
Automatically reopen after 1 to 730 days. Valid only with \fB\-\-ignore\fR.
If omitted, the existing indefinite-ignore behavior is retained.
.TP
.BI \-\-config-file\ PATH
Use an alternate runtime TOML configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-env-file\ PATH
Use an alternate environment file. Never commit it if it contains credentials.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show timestamped request and response diagnostics on standard error. The
diagnostics include the endpoint, status, elapsed time, and response size;
request bodies, credentials, and response content are not logged.
.TP
.BI \-\-log-file\ PATH
Override the default private log at
.I logs/qid.log . Rotation starts at 5 MiB
and retains three backups, limiting the log set to approximately 20 MiB. A
log is written for every normal command invocation. Each invocation starts a separate block
marked with its QID and mode, with a blank line before it.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Open the bundled manual page using the system \fBman\fR command.
.TP
.B ?
Show command help, equivalent to invoking \fBqid \-\-help\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
qid 12345 --ips "192.0.2.10-192.0.2.20"
.EE
.PP
.EX
qid 12345 --asset-ids "100001,100002"
.EE
.PP
.EX
qid 12345 --ips "192.0.2.10" --verify-ignored
.EE
.PP
.EX
qid 12345 --verify-ignored --ignored-only
.EE
.PP
.EX
qid 12345 --ips "192.0.2.10" --ignore \\
  --reopen-after-days 30 --comment "Temporary vulnerability exception"
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/runtime.toml
Default non-secret runtime settings from the installed project directory.
.TP
.I .env
Default local credentials from the installed project directory. Keep it private
and untracked.
.TP
.I .env.example
Template showing supported variables without credentials.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
.B Ignore selector required
Supply one of \fB\-\-ips\fR, \fB\-\-asset-ids\fR, or
\fB\-\-dns-hostnames\fR when using the state-changing \fB\-\-ignore\fR
workflow. Read-only lookups may omit a selector to query all assets.
.TP
.B Authentication failure
Check credentials in \fI.env\fR and the configured authentication model.
.TP
.B No matching assets
Check the exact Asset ID or DNS name as returned by Qualys Host List.
.TP
.B No detections
The supplied scope returned no matching detections for this QID; assets
outside that scope were not inspected.
.TP
.B Ignore request rejected
Check the audit comment, displayed targets, and confirmation text. No request
is submitted without exact confirmation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed, including a valid empty result.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, validation, transport, or Qualys request error.
.SH SECURITY
Credentials are read from environment variables or the local environment file
and should not be supplied as command-line arguments. Normal operation is
read-only; \fB\-\-ignore\fR is the only option that submits a state-changing
request.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python (1)
